    "how_to_repeat":  [
                          "Read LoginMessages.xml from Root.wad in your own r806919 install with `bindecode` --client \u003cinstall\u003e --text LoginMessages.xml.",
                          "Read ServiceID and ProtocolType from _ProtocolInfo/RECORD; enumerate each message RECORD and retain each non-metadata field name and its TYPE (or the supported TPYE/TYP spelling, with GlobalID inferred as GID).",
                          "Use explicit _MsgOrder or _MsgType where the first message has it; otherwise sort distinct message element tags by byte-ordinal order and number them from 1, collapsing repeated tags only when their fields match.",
                          "Run `bindecode --client \u003cinstall\u003e --sweep` as an archive-decode check; the sweep covers BINd entries, not the XML message definitions."
                      ],
    "evidence":  [
                     "`bindecode` --client \u003cinstall\u003e --text LoginMessages.xml read this definition from the local r806919 Root.wad; it declares service id 7, protocol name LOGIN, and 29 distinct ordered messages with 105 fields.",
